While [JACKSON-792](http://jira.codehaus.org/browse/JACKSON-792) did add some support for forward reference, it only handles the case where the object referenced are in "cascade" and where the pass or re-ordering properties (see [BeanDeserializerBase#deserializeWithObjectId](https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind/blob/master/src/main/java/com/fasterxml/jackson/databind/deser/BeanDeserializerBase.java#L999)) ensure that the id property is always read first. However, this isn't the case most of the time, especially when `alwaysAsId` is used during serialization; resulting json cannot be parsed back unless under very specific conditions. For example (this is actual json generated by Jackson in a test case):

```
{ "employees" : [ 
